{"availability":"available","full":"samutoljamo/g-fold","name":"g-fold","description":"Fuel Optimal Large Divert Guidance Algorithm","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":27,"forks":5,"created":"2021-10-28T19:33:52Z","updated":"2026-08-20T16:53:48Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["landing","mars","optimization-algorithms","space"],"demo":"https://samutoljamo.github.io/g-fold/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:55.444Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:55.444Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:55.444Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T21:04:55.444Z","stars":27,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["🚀 Try the interactive playground → — edit a landing config and solve it live in your browser (runs the solver via WebAssembly, no install).","G-FOLD (\"Guidance for Fuel-Optimal Large Diverts\") computes the fuel-optimal powered-descent trajectory for a landing spacecraft. A Rust core (gfold-core) poses the min-fuel soft-landing problem as a second-order cone program and solves it directly with Clarabel, exposed through a CLI, Python bindings, and a WebAssembly module from the same engine. Correctness is guarded by a CVXPY reference oracle: CI differentially tests the Rust solver against the reference within a tolerance, so the fast path stays honest.","This started as a high-school curiosity project built on cvxpy (with Clarabel as the backend) plus cvxpygen for C++ codegen. The Rust core replaces that Python + C++ stack with a single, simpler problem definition that is both faster for large horizons and trivial to bind into other languages. The original cvxpy implementation lives on as the reference oracle that keeps the new core correct."],"features":["Blackmore et al. \"Minimum-Landing-Error Powered-Descent Guidance for Mars Landing Using Convex Optimization\"","Neal et al. \"Fuel-Optimal Spacecraft Guidance for Landing in Planetary Pits\""],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/samutoljamo/g-fold/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"13a495cd6816f2a3b60d6eba6fb33a3ffebd344a79ad6896f496ca515df66ddb","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:55.765Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:55.765Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"🚀 Try the interactive playground → — edit a landing config and solve it live in your browser (runs the solver via WebAssembly, no install).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/samutoljamo/g-fold/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"13a495cd6816f2a3b60d6eba6fb33a3ffebd344a79ad6896f496ca515df66ddb","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/samutoljamo/g-fold/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:55.765Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-20T16:53:48Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/samutoljamo/g-fold/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T21:04:55.766Z","hash":"13a495cd6816f2a3b60d6eba6fb33a3ffebd344a79ad6896f496ca515df66ddb","originalBytes":3166,"storedBytes":3166,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["gfold","python","fuel-optimal","install","core","cvxpy","flight","guidance","landing","reference","rust","solve","solver","webassembly","bindings","clarabel","cli","config","default","examples","g-fold","license","npm","oracle","powered-descent","time","trajectory","al.","c++","cfg","config.json","contributing.md","edit","gfold-cli","gfold-core","landing.json","large","plot","plot.png","problem","samutoljamo","see","tests","using","above","against","any","backend","based","bind","blackmore","both","browser","build","built","cargo","codegen.","command","command-line","computes","cone","contribution","convex","correct.","correctness","crates.io","curiosity","curl","cvxpygen","defaults","definition","details.","development","differential","differentially","directly","diverts","engine.","exposed","fast","faster","fixed","generate","gfold-fixtures","gfold-py","gfold-wasm","gfold.config","gfold.solve","guarded","high-s